# Build context excludes for the add-on image.
#
# Patterns are matched against the whole path relative to this directory (the
# build context root per config.yaml), so a bare `node_modules` would only ever
# match ./node_modules. `**` matches zero or more directories, covering both the
# root case and wrapper/node_modules.
#
# wrapper/node_modules is the load-bearing one: the Dockerfile runs `npm ci`
# (COPY wrapper/package*.json -> npm ci -> COPY wrapper/) and a host-built
# node_modules would overwrite the image's linux install on the second COPY.
# CI never hits this because it builds from a fresh checkout.
**/node_modules

# Python build/test artifacts (ha-mcp deps are installed from uv.lock in-image)
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
